/** @page jsonreleasehistory json Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section json_v3_0_0 json Module Version 3.0.0

    - the json module is now delivered with %Qore itself and versions with it; it was previously
      maintained in a separate \c module-json repository
    - the JSON parser and serializer are published to other binary modules as a versioned C++ API
      in \c <qore/QoreJsonApi.h>, so a module whose own data format is JSON &mdash; the
      \c avro module, whose schemas are JSON documents &mdash; can parse and generate JSON from
      C++ without %Qore-language code; see @ref jsoncppapisecguide
    - the 16 companion user modules (A2aClient, A2aClientDataProvider, A2aServerHandler,
      FhirRestClient, FhirRestDataProvider, JsonFileDataProvider, JsonLd, JsonRpcClientIo,
      JsonRpcConnection, JsonRpcHandler, McpClient, McpClientDataProvider, McpServerHandler,
      NdjsonDataProvider, OneRecordClient and OneRecordServerHandler) ship with %Qore as well
    - network access through @ref Qore::Json::JsonRpcClient "JsonRpcClient" and filesystem access through
      @ref Qore::Json::JsonSchema::load() "JsonSchema::load()" respect the \c NETWORK and \c FILESYSTEM
      functional domains and their corresponding parse options
    - added @ref Qore::Json::jws_sign() "jws_sign()" and @ref Qore::Json::jws_verify() "jws_verify()",
      which sign and verify a caller-supplied JWS Signing Input; unlike
      @ref Qore::Json::jwt_encode() "jwt_encode()" they do not require the payload to be a JWT claims
      object, which is what JWS profiles such as the A2A protocol's signed Agent Cards need

    - added TOON (Token-Oriented Object Notation) serialization support
      (@ref Qore::Json::make_toon() "make_toon()" / @ref Qore::Json::parse_toon() "parse_toon()"); see
      @ref jsontoonserializationguide
    - added the @ref jsonrpcclientiointro "JsonRpcClientIo" module: pure-Qore JSON-RPC
      client with async I/O via HttpClientIo:
      - full JSON-RPC 1.0, 1.1, and 2.0 protocol support
      - async I/O with automatic protocol negotiation (HTTP/3, HTTP/2, HTTP/1.1) and connection pooling
      - API-compatible with the native JsonRpcClient class
      - JSON-RPC 2.0 notification support
      - debug info variants for all call methods
      - ConnectionProvider integration with \c jsonrpcio:// and \c jsonrpcios:// URL schemes
    - added the @ref fhirrestclientintro "FhirRestClient" module for HL7 FHIR JSON REST
      servers:
      - FHIR R4-compatible JSON request/response handling with \c application/fhir+json
      - \c fhir:// and \c fhirs:// ConnectionProvider schemes
      - CapabilityStatement and SMART discovery helpers
      - resource read/search/create/update/delete helpers with conditional create and ETag support
      - \c OperationOutcome exception mapping and validation/terminology delegation helpers
    - added the @ref fhirrestdataproviderintro "FhirRestDataProvider" module:
      - \c fhirrest DataProvider factory for FHIR REST server connections
      - metadata, resource CRUD/search, validation, and terminology actions
      - typed generic request/response metadata for action catalogs
      - generated FHIR R4 resource type catalog and local resource type validation
      - generated FHIR R4 \c HashDataType metadata for \c Patient, \c Observation, and \c Bundle
      - generated FHIR R4 resource-specific action metadata for typed \c Patient, \c Observation, and \c Bundle
        actions
    - added the @ref jsonldintro "JsonLd" module with full W3C JSON-LD 1.1 compliance:
      - expansion, compaction, flattening, framing algorithms
      - toRdf/fromRdf with N-Quads serialization
      - thread-safe context caching with TTL
      - pluggable document loaders (HTTP, file, caching)
      - passes 1167/1167 non-skipped W3C conformance tests
    - added the @ref onerecordclientintro "OneRecordClient" module for IATA ONE Record
      (API v2.2.0, Cargo Ontology v3.2.0):
      - REST client for air cargo data sharing via JSON-LD
      - logistics object CRUD with revision tracking
      - change request lifecycle (submit, accept, reject, revoke)
      - logistics events, audit trail, subscriptions
      - OAuth 2.0 / OpenID Connect authentication
      - ConnectionProvider integration with \c 1r:// and \c 1rs:// URL schemes
    - added the @ref onerecordserverhandlerintro "OneRecordServerHandler" module for
      ONE Record server support:
      - REST handler with full URL routing for all ONE Record API v2.2.0 endpoints
      - pluggable storage backend (abstract interface + in-memory implementation)
      - pluggable authorization (abstract interface + permissive implementation)
      - change request workflow with optimistic concurrency (revision-based)
      - webhook notification delivery via bounded thread pool
      - verification requests and access delegations
      - audit trail with per-object history
      - JSON-LD integration via the JsonLd module

    - added CBOR serialization support (make_cbor/parse_cbor)
    - added the @ref a2aclientintro "A2aClient" module for connecting to A2A agents:
      - Agent Card discovery via \c /.well-known/agent-card.json
      - Authenticated extended Agent Card retrieval
      - Message sending with task lifecycle management
      - SSE streaming for real-time task updates
      - Push notification configuration CRUD
      - Task management (get, cancel, resubscribe)
      - ConnectionProvider integration with \c a2a:// and \c a2as:// URL schemes
    - added the @ref a2aserverhandlerintro "A2aServerHandler" module for A2A server support:
      - Agent Card serving via GET \c /.well-known/agent-card.json
      - JSON-RPC dispatch for \c message/send, \c message/stream
      - Task lifecycle management with state machine validation
      - SSE streaming for real-time task updates
      - Push notification config CRUD
      - Session management
    - added the @ref a2aclientdataproviderintro "A2aClientDataProvider" module for DataProvider API:
      - factory registration for automatic data provider discovery
      - agent card providers: get and get-extended
      - message providers: send messages to agents
      - task providers: get and cancel tasks
      - event provider: observe task status/artifact/message updates
      - ConnectionProvider integration with \c a2a:// and \c a2as:// URL schemes
    - added JWT encode/decode support with HS* and RS* algorithms
    - added @ref Qore::Json::JsonSchema "JsonSchema" for JSON Schema validation, with typed
      validation results and error lists
    - added @ref Qore::Json::JsonSaxParser "JsonSaxParser" for event-based parsing and
      @ref Qore::Json::JsonStreamWriter "JsonStreamWriter" for streaming JSON output

    - added the @ref mcpclientdataproviderintro "McpClientDataProvider" module providing a
      DataProvider API for MCP servers:
      - factory registration for automatic data provider discovery
      - tools provider: list and call MCP tools
      - resources provider: list and read MCP resources
      - prompts provider: list and get MCP prompts
      - completion provider: get autocompletion suggestions
      - ping provider: verify server connectivity
      - ConnectionProvider integration for connection management
      - comprehensive type definitions, enums, and allowed values for MCP request/response fields
      - notification event provider with observer pattern support
      - constructor option metadata for MCP client name and version
    - added the @ref mcpclientintro "McpClient" module for connecting to MCP servers as a
      client:
      - full MCP protocol support with automatic version negotiation (2024-11-05 through 2025-11-25)
      - HTTP + Server-Sent Events (SSE) transport
      - tools: list and call server tools
      - resources: list and read server resources
      - prompts: list and get server prompts with arguments
      - completion: autocompletion for prompts and resources
      - logging: receive server log messages
      - event callbacks for server notifications
      - session management with \c Mcp-Session-Id header
      - ConnectionProvider integration with \c mcp:// and \c mcps:// URL schemes
    - added MCP 2025-11-25 protocol version support (latest MCP spec) to
      @ref mcpserverhandlerintro "McpServerHandler"
    - added \c completion/complete method for autocompletion of prompts and resources
    - added logging capability and \c logging/setLevel method
    - added \c resources/read handler with callback support for custom readers
    - added \c prompts/get handler with callback support for dynamic prompt generation
    - added notifications for \c resources/list_changed and \c prompts/list_changed
    - added \c unregisterTool(), \c unregisterResource(), \c unregisterPrompt() methods
    - added \c hasTools(), \c getToolNames() methods for tool management
    - added session timeout configuration and \c cleanupExpiredSessions() method
    - added \c getSessionCount() and \c getSessionInfo() for session monitoring
    - added JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) support:
      - @ref Qore::Json::json_pointer_get() "json_pointer_get()" - navigate JSON structures using JSON Pointer syntax
      - @ref Qore::Json::json_pointer_exists() "json_pointer_exists()" - check if a JSON Pointer path exists
      - @ref Qore::Json::json_pointer_escape() "json_pointer_escape()" - escape special characters in JSON Pointer
        tokens
    - added \c removeMethod(), \c hasMethod(), \c getMethodNames() to
      @ref jsonrpchandlerintro "JsonRpcHandler"
    - fixed crashes when parsing or generating deeply nested JSON;
      @ref Qore::Json::parse_json() "parse_json()" and @ref Qore::Json::make_json() "make_json()"
      now raise a \c STACK-LIMIT-EXCEEDED exception when data is nested too deeply for the thread's stack
    - JSON generation no longer copies each nested value into its parent, which took time quadratic in the nesting
      depth
    - fixed typo in MCP error message (\c 2011-11-05 -> \c 2024-11-05)
    - fixed thread safety issue with rid counter in McpServerHandler
    - fixed sprintf bug in JsonRpcHandler batch processing
    - fixed method index population bug in JsonRpcHandler
    - fixed internal method dispatch in JsonRpcHandler for private methods

    @section json_v1_9_2 json Module Version 1.9.2
    - fixed JSON number parsing for signed exponents such as \c 1.2e-05
    - tightened JSON number validation to reject malformed inputs with invalid decimals, leading zeros, or incomplete
      exponents

    @section json_v1_9_1 json Module Version 1.9.1
    - improved MCP server capabilities by making the call context available to tools as well as improving error
      handling in tool calls to provide more relevant information to the AI for error correction
    - fixed a bug where the MCP handler would crash when tools had recursive input types
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4944">issue 4944</a>)
    - fixed a bug reporting MCP tool input schemas
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4943">issue 4943</a>)

    @section json_v1_9 json Module Version 1.9
    - added support for an MCP server with the @ref mcpserverhandlerintro "McpServerHandler"
      module

    @section json_v1_8_2 json Module Version 1.8.2
    - fixed minor formatting issues in formatted JSON output for better readability and consistency
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4499">issue 4499</a>)

    @section json_v1_8_1 json Module Version 1.8.1
    - eliminated excess whitespace from compact JSON serialization
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/4459">issue 4459</a>)

    @section json_v0_1_8 json Module Version 1.8
    - fixed a bug where numbers in scientific notation could not be parsed
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3707">issue 3707</a>)
    - implemented support for serializing connection objects
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3696">issue 3696</a>)
    - fixed the return types of deserialization to avoid type stripping
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3432">issue 3432</a>)
    - fixed output of excess noise in floating-point values
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3375">issue 3375</a>)
    - updated the @ref jsonrpcconnectionintro "JsonRpcConnection" module to support the
      updated abstract connection API
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2628">issue 2628</a>)
    - added support for serializing intervals to strings that can be manually converted to the original value
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/3135">issue 3135</a>)

    @section json_v0_1_7 json Module Version 1.7
    - deprecated support for the non-published JSON-RPC 1.1 protocol
    - added support for JSON-RPC 2.0
    - added the @ref jsonrpcconnectionintro "JsonRpcConnection" user module
    - improved argument error messages with RPC calls in the
      @ref jsonrpchandlerintro "JsonRpcHandler" module
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2573">issue 2573</a>)
    - fixed date serialization to use ISO-8601 format (instead of near-ISO-8601 format
      <a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2655">issue 2655</a>)

    @section json_v0_1_6 json Module Version 1.6
    - @ref Qore::Json::parse_json() "parse_json()" now ignores UTF-8 and Unicode BOMs at the start of passed JSON string
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/1398">issue 1398</a>)
    - fixed a bug in request logging in the @ref jsonrpchandlerintro "JsonRpcHandler" module
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/1487">issue 1487</a>)
    - fixed a bug serializing hash keys with embedded quotes
      (<a href="https://github.com/qorelanguage/qore/issues/2242">issue 2242</a>)

    @section json_v0_1_5 json Module Version 1.5
    - serialize binary values as base64-encoded strings
    - user modules moved to top-level qore module directory from version-specific module directory since they are
      valid for multiple versions of qore
    - serialize nan, +/-inf as \c null according to the JSON spec
    - added detection for invalid JSON-RPC calls and added a more user-friendly error message in the
      @ref jsonrpchandlerintro "JsonRpcHandler" module
    - new functions added conforming to %Qore's function naming convention, old camel-case functions deprecated
    - JSON tests ported to QUnit
    - %Qore 0.8.12 required as a minimum to build
    - JSON output is more compact; less extraneous whitespace is used

    @section json_v0_1_4 json Module Version 1.4

    - date/time values are always serialized with microseconds and in the local time zone for consistency's sake
    - fixed a crashing bug in the JSON control-character encoding algorithm
    - updated the @ref jsonrpchandlerintro "JsonRpcHandler" module for enhanced logging
    - source released under the MIT license as well as LGPL 2.1

    @section json_v0_1_3 json Module Version 1.3

    - always include \c charset=utf-8 in the \c Content-Type in @ref Qore::Json::JsonRpcClient "JsonRpcClient"; JSON
      messages are always serialized with UTF-8 encoding

    @section json_v0_1_2 json Module Version 1.2

    - fixed serialization/deserialization/escaping regarding control characters

    @section json_v0_1_1 json Module Version 1.1

    - added support for the new arbitrary-precision numeric type introduced in qore 0.8.6
    - serialize control characters with escape codes to be compatible with common Javascript JSON libraries (also
      corresponding deserialization support)

    @section json_v0_1_0 json Module Version 1.0

    - Initial release of the json module
    - Requires qore 0.8.1+ to build and run
*/
